  "seoBody": "<p>Your firm can have many people on the dashboard. Each one is an <strong>admin</strong> or a <strong>member</strong>.</p><h2>Roles</h2><p>Admins and members can both see users, Checks and Records. Only admins can do these:</p><ul><li>Add or remove users</li><li>Build or edit Checks</li><li>Send Checks</li><li>Handle billing and plan</li><li>Invite or remove team members</li><li>Change someone's role</li></ul><h2>Inviting someone</h2><ol><li>Go to <strong>Team</strong> on the dashboard.</li><li>Type their email address. Click <strong>Invite</strong>.</li><li>They get a link by email. It works for 7 days.</li></ol><p>New people join as admins. Change their role after they accept.</p><h2>Changing roles</h2><p>Click the role toggle by their name. You cannot demote yourself if you are the only admin.</p><h2>Removing someone</h2><p>Click <strong>Remove</strong> by their name. Their access stops at once. What they did before stays.</p><p>Still stuck? Email <a href=\"mailto:hello@quickler.co\">hello@quickler.co</a>. We reply within one business day.</p>",
